.TH THUMTOO-PREPARE 1 "2026-09-16" "thumtoo" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
thumtoo-prepare \- probe sizes and optionally warm soft ladder / tile cache
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B thumtoo-prepare
[\fIOPTION\fR]...
\fIPATH\fR...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Register paths in the thumtoo Store cache and measure native image dimensions.
Default is size-only (no soft/tiles) so cold size probes can be timed without a
GUI host. Optionally encode durable soft previews and Galapix-style 256\(mu256
JPEG tile pyramids so viewers (galapix, biltoo) can open without on-demand
encode cost.
.PP
Work is done in phases printed on stderr (unless
.BR \-q ):
.TP
.B phase 1: size probe
One job per URI. Reads the source only when size is not already in the Store;
otherwise a cache hit. Lines look like
.BI [probe " n/N] " status "  " URI "  " WxH .
Status
.B incomplete
means size is stored (normal after a successful probe).
.B ready
means soft/full content was already considered ready.
.B failed
means the probe could not obtain dimensions.
Phase end prints wall_ms, ok/fail, and probes_per_s.
.B Sequential
archives (RAR/CBR, tar, solid 7z) share one extract cursor per file — extra
.B \-\-jobs
do not parallelize members of the same archive.
.TP
.B phase 2: soft ladder
Only with
.BR \-\-ladder .
Encodes a durable preview at the requested long edge.
.TP
.B phase 2 or 3: tile pyramid
Only with
.BR \-\-tiles .
Builds the multi-scale 256\(mu256 JPEG pyramid (plain files and archive members).
.PP
Stdout ends with a one-line Store tally (blobs, locators, media, tiles).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress per-job progress on stderr.
.TP
.BI \-\-cache " DIR"
Cache root (default:
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/thumtoo
or
.IR ~/.cache/thumtoo ).
.TP
.BI \-\-ladder " EDGE"
After probes, encode one soft preview per URI (largest policy edge \(<= EDGE).
.TP
.B \-\-tiles
After probes, build tile pyramids for each sized URI.
.TP
.BI \-\-min\-scale " N"
Finest tile scale to generate (default: 0 = full resolution).
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-scale " M"
Coarsest tile scale (default: \-1 = until single-tile coverage).
.TP
.B \-\-stats
Print detailed timings on stderr (implied by
.B \-\-tiles
/
.BR \-\-ladder ).
.TP
.B \-\-stats\-line
One-line timings (script-friendly).
.TP
.BI \-\-jobs " N"
Worker threads (default: CPUs, max 32).
.TP
.BR \-\-sizes\-only ", " \-\-size\-only
Size probes only (default when no
.BR \-\-tiles / \-\-ladder / \-\-lqip ).
Prints wall time and throughput; no soft or tile phase.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-cache
Ephemeral Store: three SQLite
.B :memory:
databases (index/bulk/user). Nothing is written under
.BR \-\-cache .
Use for pure cold-probe timing without durable Store I/O.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B non-zero
Usage error or fatal exception.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
# Time cold size probes only (no biltoo):
thumtoo-prepare --sizes-only --no-cache /path/to/archive.rar
thumtoo-prepare --sizes-only --stats /path/to/archive.rar
thumtoo-prepare --sizes-only --jobs 1 /path/to/archive.rar
thumtoo-prepare --tiles /path/to/album/
thumtoo-prepare --tiles /path/to/archive.rar
thumtoo-prepare --ladder 512 --tiles photo.jpg
thumtoo-status path photo.jpg
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR thumtoo (7),
.BR thumtoo-status (1),
.BR thumtoo-tile (1),
.BR thumtoo-gc (1),
.BR thumtoo-archive (1),
.BR thumtoo-bench (1)
